        {
          "height" : 13.2,
          "text" : "2. Method",
          "width" : 51.8,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 185.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 12.1,
          "text" : "2.1. The test slot",
          "width" : 75.8,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 205.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "A folded card spacer fixes the height of a model rail above",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 216.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "its baseboard. We measured spacers folded from three card",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 228.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "stocks in a single test slot and compared the measured",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 240.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "heights with a simple layer model. The model predicts the",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 252.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "height of a folded spacer to within a tenth of a millimetre",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 264.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "when the crease allowance is taken from a two-layer trial.",
          "width" : 236.2,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 276.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "We describe the slot, the measurement procedure and the",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 288.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "remaining sources of error, and we list practical rules for",
          "width" : 236.2,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 300.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "choosing a card stock for a given rail height.",
          "width" : 179.2,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 312.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "The slot was cut into a block of laminated board and lined",
          "width" : 236.2,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 223.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "with a strip of thin brass so that the card could not dent the",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 235.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "walls. A sliding rail of known height rests on top of the",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 247.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "spacer, and the height is read from a scale on the side of the",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 259.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "block. The block was clamped to the bench throughout the",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 271.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "trial so that the scale did not move between readings.",
          "width" : 211.4,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 283.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Each spacer was inserted with its folded edge towards",
          "width" : 224.3,
          "x" : 329.2,
          "y" : 295.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "the back of the slot. The rail was lowered onto it and left",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 307.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "for ten seconds before the reading was taken, because a",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 319.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "freshly folded spacer springs back slowly. Three readings",
          "width" : 236.2,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 331.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "were taken for each spacer, removing and reinserting it be-",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 343.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "tween readings.",
          "width" : 62.5,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 355.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 13.2,
          "text" : "1. Introduction",
          "width" : 76.8,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 361.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 12.1,
          "text" : "2.2. Layer model",
          "width" : 78.3,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 375.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Paper models of railways need many small parts of exact",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 387.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "height. Rails, platform edges and signal bases all sit on",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 399.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "spacers, and a spacer that is too thick by a fraction of a",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 411.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "millimetre lifts a rail joint enough to derail a light wagon.",
          "width" : 236.2,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 423
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Most builders cut spacers from card and fold them until they",
          "width" : 236.2,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 435
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "reach the height they want [3]. Folding is quick and needs",
          "width" : 236.2,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 446.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "no tools, but the height of a folded spacer is not simply the",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 458.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "sum of the card thicknesses: each crease adds a small al-",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 470.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "lowance, and the allowance depends on the card and on how",
          "width" : 236.2,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 482.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "firmly the crease is pressed.",
          "width" : 110.9,
          "x" : 58.5,
          "y" : 494.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "We model the height h of a spacer with n layers of card of",
          "width" : 236.3,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 393.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.1,
          "text" : "thickness t as",
          "width" : 54,
          "x" : 317.3,
          "y" : 405.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.6,
          "text" : "h= n t + (n− 1) c,",
